## 2. OPEN BOX DELIVERY (OBD) VERIFICATION
> **NPCI UDIR Section 3.2 / Visa CE 3.0 Section 3.2b — OBD Protocol**

This order was fulfilled via **Open Box Delivery (OBD)**. Under NPCI and Visa guidelines:

- The courier **opened the package at the doorstep** in the presence of the cardholder.
- The cardholder **physically inspected** the product for condition, completeness, and conformity.
- The cardholder then **entered the delivery OTP** to confirm acceptance after inspection.
- **OTP Verification:** {% if otp_verified %}**[VERIFIED — CUSTOMER ACCEPTED AFTER INSPECTION]**{% else %}**[NOT VERIFIED]**{% endif %}

Per NPCI UDIR Section 3.2, the OTP entered after open-box inspection constitutes **LEGAL ACKNOWLEDGEMENT** that the customer verified the product's condition. The burden of proof shifts to the cardholder to demonstrate the defect was not observable during doorstep inspection.

